# Rust
/target

# Tauri build artifacts (schemas regenerated by tauri-build on every build).
# gen/android is real source (Gradle project + future Kotlin plugins) and IS tracked;
# its build outputs are covered by gen/android/.gitignore.
crates/solum-app/gen/schemas/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig

# Local Solum data (never commit personal data — privacy is architectural, see ARCHITECTURE.md §4)
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/data
solum.sqlite*
# Any other local sqlite databases (e.g. demo.sqlite from CLI walkthroughs) and their WAL/SHM files
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Local LLM credentials (API keys must never be committed)
solum-llm.json

# Generic local configuration and private-key material. Keep shareable examples
# explicitly named (for example, .env.example) rather than checking in values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
service-account*.json
credentials*.json
*secrets*.json

# Soulous dual-token session (user-owned service; local-only credentials)
solum-soulous.json

# Mail connector credentials: app passwords / OAuth refresh tokens are
# local-only and must never be put into SQLite, sync, exports, or Git.
solum-email.json

# Sync: client config holds the pre-shared master key; server db holds blobs
solum-sync.json
pa-sync.sqlite*

# Android release signing key (self-use sideload). Losing this file means
# future app updates can't overwrite the installed one (uninstall required,
# local device data lost) — back it up somewhere durable, outside git.
*.keystore
*.jks
keystore.properties

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
Solum_demo.mp4
Solum_demo_script_v2.md

# AI agent skill tooling (local dev aid, not project source — see docs/MISC.md 2026-07-15)
.claude/
.agents/
.impeccable/
skills-lock.json

# Private competition material — do not include project or contributor
# documentation in the public source snapshot.
/docs/
/README.md
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
